<title>PORTUGAL: Most Portuguese firms see euro as neutral - poll.</title>
<headline>Most Portuguese firms see euro as neutral - poll.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>More than 50 percent of Portuguese businesses polled by the Portuguese Industrial Association (AIP) said the introduction of the EU's single currency in 1999 would be neutral for them while 39 percent thought it would be positive.</p>
<p>Ten percent of the 861 companies contacted by AIP thought the euro would have a negative impact.</p>
<p>The larger the company, the more likely it was to take a positive attitude toward the euro, according to AIP.</p>
<p>Fifty-three percent of companies with more than 500 workers were enthusiastic about the single currency while smaller firms working in domestic construction, retail and services tended to be more wary.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
